frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# The Esteso 1964 guitar body with its bridge, data/instruments/geometry/guitar-esteso-1964-zimmer2024/
# shell-assembly-h12-bridge.tsv (20 parts, 5907 nodes, 10468 triangles, 22 ties): the h12 table regenerated by
# crates/fs-couple/examples/guitar_body_modes/gen_shell_assembly.py with bridge=1, which adds the printed rosewood bridge
# as a wall on the top's outer skin (its meta row "bridge_model"). The options are those of the Esteso cost rung
# (crates/fs-couple/examples/material_strings/body/shell/tests.rs, esteso_profile). Body modes from 15 Hz (above the free
# body's rigid motion) to 2 kHz, the guitar shell packs' declared angular-frequency validity. The table omits the neck and
# heel, the blocks, the linings, the rosette and the fingerboard (its meta row "omitted").
window-hz 15 2000
projection-work 549755813888
# The performance body record's thickness [m]; every part's own thickness is written as a ratio to it.
reference-thickness-m 0.0025
# Spruce (the top and its braces) is the performance body pack; the FPL-GTR-282 rosewood and cedar shell packs are the
# others, as the table's parts name them.
pack spruce @body
pack rosewood guitar-rosewood-brazilian-fpl-gtr282-bremaud2011-shell.fsmatpk
pack cedar guitar-cedar-western-red-fpl-gtr282-shell.fsmatpk
# The string meets the top at the table's own drive row "outer string, +y side" (the treble E): (x, y) [m] of the table's frame, driving along the top normal.
# x = 0.33454 is the table's inferred drive station (u-bridge-position), 2.8 mm from the drawn bridge's centre; the saddle hairline from the printed scale is 8.1 mm toward the neck.
bridge-component top
bridge-direction 0 0 1
bridge 0.33454 0.02925
